{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S5 (6755) PS2: fixed Verified-1 CLI-reference drift gate. Root cause: live intercept-parser --help is Python-version-sensitive (3.13 argparse metavar-collapse '--output, -o {x}' + mutually-exclusive usage-group wrapping) but the drift gate runs on the 3.11/3.12/3.13 matrix. Fix: canonicalize intercept render (_unwrap_usage single-line usage + _collapse_metavars to single-metavar form). Verified byte-identical --check under 3.11(uv)+3.12+3.13.15. Added RED-first regression oracle (usage-unwrapped, metavars-collapsed). LLM-Review+1 on PS1 was cleared by the real code change; both bots re-run."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787313741676027001,"uuid":"f10aa400-8357-4b07-aa4a-512d983628cf"}